EXT. DRAGON'S ROOST - MOUNTAIN LEDGE - DAWN

A windswept ledge high on a black peak. Clouds boil below. In the distance, a thin line of silver: the sea.

Four adventurers climb the last switchback: SIR OSWIN HARTLEY (40s, battered plate armor), the thief PETRONELLA "NELLA" FINCH (20s, hooded, quick-eyed), the mage ZAHARA QUDSI (30s, indigo robes, staff topped with a glowing crystal) and the young squire BASIL THORNWICK (14, carrying too many packs).

OSWIN
Quiet now. We approach.

NELLA
I'm always quiet.

ZAHARA
You hummed all night.

NELLA
Only softly.

BASIL
Sir, my pack is on fire.

OSWIN
What?

BASIL
Only a little.

Zahara flicks her fingers; the flame hisses out. A deep rumble shakes the ledge. Pebbles skitter down the rock. The adventurers freeze.

OSWIN
That was the mountain, wasn't it?

ZAHARA
That was something else.

A great shadow slides across them. A growl like grinding stones rolls down from above.

Oswin draws his sword. Nella melts into the rocks. Basil drops his packs.

Then, from the cave mouth ahead, a figure steps into the light: TAMARISK ODEN (60s, patched green cloak, a ring of keys at her belt), the dragon's keeper, holding a bucket.

TAMARISK
Oh, don't mind him. He hasn't had his tea.

OSWIN
His tea?

TAMARISK
Chamomile. Dry throat. Come in.
